        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U36 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36 wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled according to the listed sourcing part numbers, the e-stop outputs may actively drive the sink lines rather than provide the intended open-drain behavior, compromising the e-stop interface and its fail-safe operation.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["SW6", "R34", "R35"],
      "pins": ["SW6.1", "SW6.2", "SW6.3", "SW6.4", "R34.1", "R34.2", "R35.1", "R35.2"],
      "nets": ["/CAN0_N", "/CAN0_P", "/CAN1_N", "/CAN1_P", "Net-(R34-Pad2)", "Net-(R35-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "Closing the two SW6 DIP contacts connects CAN0_P directly to CAN1_P and connects CAN0_N to CAN1_N through R34 and R35 in series.",
      "expected": "CAN0 and CAN1 should remain separate buses; any termination/configuration switches should not cross-connect their signal pairs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_P ... SW6.4(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_P ... SW6.3(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(2,passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With the switches closed, the two CAN interfaces are no longer independent and can interfere with each other when connected to separate buses.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are supported by the netlist: the CAN transceiver grounds bypass the stated isolation, the e-stop buffer sourcing fields specify a different output type than the intended open-drain part, and SW6 can cross-connect the two CAN buses."
}

